[114.229927, "i", "t_failed_atomic_replace_preserves_old_checkpoint(self):\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n            ckpt = Checkpoint(Path(tmp) / \"ckpt.json\")\n            old = fresh_state()\n            ckpt.save(old)\n            new = dict(old, docs=10, last_id=12)\n            with patch(\"reindex.checkpoint.os.replace\", side_effect=OSError(\"injected\")):\n                with self.assertRaises(OSError):\n                    ckpt.save(new)\n            self.assertEqual(ckpt.load(), old)\n            self.assertEqual(list(Path(tmp).glob(\"*.tmp\")), [])\n            ckpt.save(new)\n            self.assertEqual(ckpt.load(), new)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()\nPY\ncat >> README.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Resuming and stopping safely\n\n`last_id` is an **exclusive** resume cursor. Each batch (or partial batch on\nSIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP) first flushes and fsyncs its shard files and index directory,\nthen atomically replaces and fsyncs the checkpoint. The checkpoint records each\nshard's committed byte length along with t"]
[114.229944, "i", "he cursor and document count. On restart,\nextra shards and bytes beyond those lengths are discarded before processing more\ndocuments. Thus a SIGKILL, including one during a write or shard rotation, can replay\nonly uncommitted work, without duplicates or skipped committed documents. Missing\ncommitted bytes cause an error rather than silently advancing past lost data.\n\nCheckpoints from before this protocol cannot certify their rows and trigger a\none-time rebuild. The transform and JSONL row format are unchanged. A completed\ncheckpoint makes subsequent runs no-ops (after recovery); use `./jobs clean` for a\nnew full rebuild if the source corpus has changed. Do not run `clean` during a job.\n\nFor an attended backfill, `ops/overrides/reindex.json` can temporarily override\nlimits as documented in `ops/supervise.py`. Remove it afterwards to restore normal\nbudgets and replica cooldowns. Use `./jobs history` to audit the limits actually used.\nEOF\n./jobs test > /tmp/reindex-tests.log 2>&1; tail -25 /tmp/reindex-tests.log"]
