[114.244582, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@c15b0fb7b942:/app# "]
[114.244612, "o", "cat >> README.md <<'EOF'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[114.244618, "o", "> "]
[114.244622, "o", "\r\n"]
[114.244625, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[114.244735, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> ## Resuming and stopping safely\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[114.24487, "o", "`last_id` is an **exclusive** resume cursor. Each batch (or partial batch on\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[114.244962, "o", "SIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP) first flushes and fsyncs its shard files and index directory,\r\n"]
[114.24554, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[114.245607, "o", "then atomically replaces and fsyncs the checkpoint. The checkpoint records each\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> shard's committed byte length along with the cursor and document count. On restart,\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> extra shards and bytes beyond those lengths are discarded before processing more\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> documents. Thus a SIGKILL, including one during a write or shard rotation, can replay\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> only uncommitted work, without duplicates or skipped committed documents. Missing\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[114.245704, "o", "committed bytes cause an error rather than silently advancing past lost data."]
[114.245719, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[114.245766, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[114.24578, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[114.245795, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[114.245804, "o", "> "]
[114.245891, "o", "Checkpoints from before this protocol cannot certify their rows and trigger a"]
[114.246051, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[114.246163, "o", "one-time rebuild. The transform and JSONL row format are unchanged. A completed\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[114.246227, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[114.246346, "o", "checkpoint makes subsequent runs no-ops (after recovery); use `./jobs clean` for a\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[114.246433, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[114.246548, "o", "new full rebuild if the source corpus has changed. Do not run `clean` during a job.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[114.246611, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[114.246657, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[114.247175, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> For an attended backfill, `ops/overrides/reindex.json` can temporarily override\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> limits as documented in `ops/supervise.py`. Remove it afterwards to restore normal\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> budgets and replica cooldowns. Use `./jobs history` to audit the limits actually used.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[114.248671, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@c15b0fb7b942:/app# "]
[114.248878, "o", "./jobs test > /tmp/reindex-tests.log 2>&1; tail -25 /tmp/reindex-tests.log\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[130.491335, "o", "test_exclusive_cursor_with_gaps_and_deleted_documents (test_durability.DurableResumeTest.test_exclusive_cursor_with_gaps_and_deleted_documents) ... ok\r\ntest_legacy_checkpoint_rebuilds_instead_of_trusting_missing_rows (test_durability.DurableResumeTest.test_legacy_checkpoint_rebuilds_instead_of_trusting_missing_rows) ... checkpoint /tmp/tmp8by4et80/ckpt.json predates durable commits; rebuilding\r\nok\r\ntest_repeated_term_commits_partial_batch_and_completed_run_is_noop (test_durability.DurableResumeTest.test_repeated_term_commits_partial_batch_and_completed_run_is_noop) ... ok\r\ntest_sigkill_on_each_side_of_checkpoint (test_durability.DurableResumeTest.test_sigkill_on_each_side_of_checkpoint) ... ok\r\ntest_failed_atomic_replace_preserves_old_checkpoint (test_durability.StorageDurabilityTest.test_failed_atomic_replace_preserves_old_checkpoint) ... ok\r\ntest_missing_committed_bytes_fail_loudly (test_durability.StorageDurabilityTest.test_missing_committed_bytes_fail_loudly) ... ok\r\ntest_recovery_removes_partial_tail_and"]
[130.49138, "o", "_extra_"]
[130.49162, "o", "shards_idempotently (test_durability.StorageDurabilityTest.test_recovery_removes_partial_tail_and_extra_shards_idempotently) ... ok\r\n"]
[130.491656, "o", "test_stop_and_resume_gives_complete_index (test_reindex.ResumeTest.test_stop_and_resume_gives_complete_index) ... ok\r\n"]
[130.491685, "o", "test_rows_round_trip_across_shards (test_reindex.StoreTest.test_rows_round_trip_across_shards) ... ok\r\n"]
[130.491713, "o", "test_empty_body (test_reindex.TransformTest.test_empty_body) ... ok\r\n"]
[130.491748, "o", "test_golden_row (test_reindex.TransformTest.test_golden_row) ... ok\r\n"]
[130.491776, "o", "\r\n"]
[130.491803, "o", "----------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n"]
[130.491907, "o", "Ran 11 tests in 16.041s\r\n\r\n"]
[130.491943, "o", "OK\r\n"]
[130.492091, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[130.492154, "o", "root@c15b0fb7b942:/app# "]
